WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
This is what developing the Finance
Accounting Book app in a terminal can look like.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
We open the project folder.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.000
React and TypeScript power the interface, Python runs
the server, and a local SQLite database stores the records.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
During development, we edit individual pages,
such as the income and expense overview.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.000
The npm run build command
builds the web interface.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Then we enter the server folder
and run serve.py.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The Accounting Book opens
at the local address on port 5175.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Code and commands become a clear,
practical app for personal finances.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
This is an illustrative demonstration
with fictional data.
